WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.786
Every partner relationship has one record,

2
00:00:02.786 --> 00:00:06.587
written before access is granted
and kept as evidence after.

3
00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:10.602
It lives in the repository beside
the configuration it describes,

4
00:00:10.602 --> 00:00:13.813
so a change to either arrives
in the same pull request.

5
00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:19.706
It has six sections: authority and purpose,
owners, risk, agreement and assurance,

6
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:24.974
route and user type, lifecycle and
operations, and the readiness checks.

7
00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:27.337
Three rules apply to every field.

8
00:00:27.337 --> 00:00:31.509
Reference, don't copy: the
agreement, the privacy determination

9
00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:35.199
and the records schedule go
in as identifiers and dates.

10
00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:39.084
One decider: each readiness
check names the business owner,

11
00:00:39.084 --> 00:00:42.650
and the authorizing official
is consulted on the last.

12
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.450
And a blank is a finding: write none
or not applicable, with a reason.

13
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:52.619
The Entra profile adds the values the
record asks for: tenant relationship,

14
00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:56.203
cross-tenant settings,
configuration IDs, mappings,

15
00:00:56.203 --> 00:01:00.038
access governance, validation
results and monitoring.

16
00:01:00.038 --> 00:01:05.500
The record holds no personal data about
individual partner persons, and no secrets.
